            note: "ながら joins two actions one person does at the same time: 音楽を聞きながら勉強します. The main action comes last and the ながら verb is the side activity, so 勉強しながら音楽を聞く puts the focus on the music. Both actions must have the same subject — for \"while my mom was cooking, I...\" use 間 / 間に or とき instead, the classic mistake. Tense goes on the final verb only (歩きながら話した). It can also describe a longer parallel situation: 働きながら大学に通う (go to college while working).",
            examples: [("歩きながらスマホを見るのは危ないです。", "It's dangerous to look at your phone while walking."), ("コーヒーを飲みながら、友達と話しました。", "I talked with my friend over coffee."), ("昼間は働きながら、夜は大学に通っています。", "I work during the day and go to university at night.")],
